stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    state "Record created, not activated" as DRAFT
    state "Activated, joining date in the future" as PRE_JOINING
    state "In service" as ACTIVE
    state "Absent without pay for a whole period" as UNPAID
    state "Suspended pending enquiry" as SUSPENDED
    state "Serving notice" as NOTICE
    state "Absconding, notice to return issued" as ABSCOND
    state "Last working day passed, settlement due" as EXITED
    state "Settlement paid and statutory closure done" as SETTLED
    state "Death in service" as DECEASED

    [*] --> DRAFT: ST1 record created from offer or import
    DRAFT --> PRE_JOINING: ST2 activated with a future joining date
    DRAFT --> ACTIVE: ST3 activated on or after the joining date
    PRE_JOINING --> ACTIVE: ST4 joining date reached and joining confirmed
    PRE_JOINING --> DRAFT: ST5 joiner does not report, activation reversed before any wage
    ACTIVE --> UNPAID: ST6 approved unpaid absence covering a whole wage period
    UNPAID --> ACTIVE: ST7 return to work recorded
    ACTIVE --> SUSPENDED: ST8 suspension ordered, recorded with its authority
    SUSPENDED --> ACTIVE: ST9 suspension revoked or enquiry closed without separation
    SUSPENDED --> NOTICE: ST10 separation decided at the end of the enquiry
    ACTIVE --> NOTICE: ST11 resignation or termination notice accepted
    ACTIVE --> ABSCOND: ST12 unauthorised absence past the tenant policy threshold
    ABSCOND --> ACTIVE: ST13 employee returns and the absence is regularised
    ABSCOND --> EXITED: ST14 abandonment concluded after the recorded notice to return
    NOTICE --> ACTIVE: ST15 resignation withdrawn before the last working day, accepted
    NOTICE --> EXITED: ST16 last working day passed
    ACTIVE --> EXITED: ST17 exit without notice, including end of a fixed term
    ACTIVE --> DECEASED: ST18 death in service recorded
    NOTICE --> DECEASED: ST18 the same during notice
    EXITED --> SETTLED: ST19 settlement paid and date of exit marked at the portal
    DECEASED --> SETTLED: ST20 nominee settlement paid and claims raised
    SETTLED --> [*]

    note right of ABSCOND
        Wages follow the days actually paid.
        Unpaid days become NCP days in the
        month's ECR line. No status is set by
        a side effect of any other action.
    end note

    note right of EXITED
        A rehire is a new employment under the
        same person, never a return to ACTIVE.
        Corrections to the exit date follow the
        typed-change rules and may need a
        joint declaration at EPFO.
    end note
